# BidWar Operation Manual — Proportional Documentation

The canonical operational knowledge base is `docs/BIDWAR_OPERATION_MANUAL.md`.

Update the manual only when the implemented change materially alters documented user-facing behaviour, operating procedures, routes, permissions, settings, or supported workflows. Update only affected sections and the change log, using verified implementation as the source.

Do not update the manual for purely internal refactors, formatting, tests, dependency maintenance, or visual-only adjustments that do not change documented operation.

Run `pnpm run check:manual` after changing the manual or its validator. This structural check does not prove that manual statements are factually correct.

For task execution, follow `docs/AI_AGENT_EXECUTION_CONTRACT.md`. This rule is not a reason to stop otherwise-complete implementation work.
